# ===========================================================================
#  config/paths_local.R.example
#
#  Copy this file to config/paths_local.R and edit it to point at your own
#  copies of the source data.  config/paths_local.R is git-ignored, so no
#  machine-specific path ends up in the published repository.
#
#  Every variable below takes precedence over the default in config.R, and
#  is itself overridden by the corresponding environment variable
#  (DMPMR_<UPPERCASE NAME>, e.g. DMPMR_BCAC_SUS_META).
#
#  ENCODING -- please keep this file ASCII-only where you can, and if any
#  data directory really does contain non-ASCII characters, save the file as
#  UTF-8 (no BOM).  config.R loads it with a UTF-8-aware reader that falls
#  back gracefully on machines whose native R locale is not UTF-8, but a file
#  re-saved in a legacy codepage (e.g. GBK/CP936) cannot be recovered.
# ===========================================================================

